  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From Research to Practice (RTP): Using Knowledge to Accelerate Progress in the Elimination of Child Labor and Forced Labor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Research to Practice (RTP) Project applies rigorous research methods in an effort to accelerate global action against child labor and forced labor. The project seeks to help policymakers and practitioners access relevant research and evaluation tools, identifies key knowledge gaps, and facilitates the development of a global research agenda to guide new policy-relevant research efforts. To that end, the project also seeks to broaden and diversify the researcher pool, increasing both the number and capacity of researchers working to shed light on these abusive labor practices.</narrative>
  </description>
